                <pb facs="0094" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1515: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-13T14:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.16
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>68. I am requested by President Menocal to extend to General Crowder an
                    invitation in his name to come to Cuba at his earliest convenience to act in the
                    capacity explained in my telegram of February 12, 11 a.m., and also to inform
                    the Department that I allow [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] this under
                    authorization from the President. Will the Department present the invitation and
                    communicate the reply?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
